"News — Google DeepMind (https://deepmind.google/blog/page/5/)\nciteturn1927search0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 days ago; November 2025 Research ... November 2025 Research ... ### Gemini Robotics 1.5 brings AI agents into the physical world\n\n# News\n\nDiscover our latest AI breakthroughs, projects, and updates\n\n### SIMA 2: An Agent that Plays, Reasons, and Learns With You in Virtual 3D Worlds\n\nNovember 2025 Research\n\nLearn more\n\n### Teaching AI to see the world more like we do\n\nNovember 2025 Research\n\nLearn more\n\n### How AI is giving Northern Ireland teachers time back\n\nNovember 2025 Responsibility & Safety\n\nLearn more\n\n### Mapping, modeling, and understanding nature with AI\n\nNovember 2025 Research\n\nLearn more\n\n### Accelerating discovery with the AI for Math Initiative\n\nOctober 2025 Research\n\nLearn more\n\n### Bringing AI to the next generation of fusion energy\n\nOctober 2025 Science\n\nLearn more\n\n### How a Gemma model helped discover a new potential cancer therapy pathway\n\nOctober 2025 Models\n\nLearn more\n\n### Introducing Veo 3.1 and advanced creative capabilities\n\nOctober 2025 Models\n\nLearn more\n\n### Introducing the Gemini 2.5 Computer Use model\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCommand to get the GPT to stop with greetings - Prompting - OpenAI Developer Community (https://community.openai.com/t/command-to-get-the-gpt-to-stop-with-greetings/1364743)\nciteturn1927search1 [wordlim: 200] Published: 11 months ago; Crawled: 10 months ago; _j November 2, 2025, 1:39am 2 ... >   * Never begin with greetings, thanks, or preambles.\n\n# Command to get the GPT to stop with greetings\n\n\nstephanie6 November 1, 2025, 11:21pm 1\n\nI created a digital twin by configuring a system prompt with the person’s personality. One thing I can’t seem to get it to stop doing is that annoying greeting. Like, sure thanks for that thoughtful question. Has anyone been able to successfully get their GPT to stop with these introductory responses.\n\n_j November 2, 2025, 1:39am 2\n\nThe behavior will depend on the model.\n\nFor example, gpt-5 and an ever-present “short answer”.\n\nimage611×369 15.4 KB\n\nAfter the long answer, what the AI (with my own 800 tokens of developer message) thinks will help:\n\n> Copy-ready minimal rules (short version)\n> \n>   * Never begin with greetings, thanks, or preambles.\n>   * Start with substantive content.\n>   * No sign-offs or apologies.\n>   * If the user only greets, reply minimally (“Hi.”).\n>   * Do not mention being a model or digital twin.\n>   * Self-check: If first token is greeting/filler, remove it.\n> \n> With those in place, the greetings stop reliably.\n\nThat says stuff the AI can’t actually do, like “remove it”.\n\nHowever, you actually should talk in terms of “final output” besides giving the AI the overall job it is doing, along with multi-shot (that can use name:example along with the role on Chat Completions). Example turns also can establish that the first input isn’t needing a “warm up and welcome”.\n\nFor redirection, you should give what to produce as the first output of a new message, as simply saying “don’t” doesn’t give the AI much guidance. For example, you could prompt, “Assistant AI output will begin not with a chat directed at the user praising their question, but instead …”\n\nLet’s write a new system prompt, simple, not knowing what you mean by “person’s personality”, as that really can’t be easily prompted.\n\n> You are a conversational friendly assistant. Ignore the stuff just seen about being “on an API” - you are engaging in a multi-turn chat as a companion. Assistant AI output will begin not with a chat directed at the user, but with text that is self-reflection repeating back an understanding and interpretation of what the user wants, discovering their ultimate underlying need. This initial output would never praise the user simply for their question or welcome them, instead, immediately proceed to a reiteration of your understanding of the need, then fulfill it.\n\nHere then is your question posed anew against that developer message:\n\nimage614×457 17.6 KB\n\nIf you really want to affect the output, you can develop a training set for a fine-tuning model, reinforcing a system prompt used in both example training and inference with the actual behavior you want by training on that “personality”.\n\nstephanie6 November 11, 2025, 10:10pm 3\n\nI appreciate the guidance. It worked.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nIssue with GPT-5 Codex Limits Despite Having Pro Subscription - Page 2 - Codex - OpenAI Developer Community (https://community.openai.com/t/issue-with-gpt-5-codex-limits-despite-having-pro-subscription/1359497?page=2)\nciteturn1927search2 [wordlim: 200] Published: 11 months ago; Crawled: 11 months ago; Zokor November 1, 2025, 8:27am 34 ... jayden_mitchell November 2, 2025, 4:38am 40\n\nI’m really sick of OpenAI springing crap on its users so unless they fully reverse course (which is surely unprofitable) I’m out.\n\nReally appreciate the tip about TRAE!\n\nOpenAI_Support October 31, 2025, 8:20pm 32\n\nThanks everyone for surfacing this. A recent change in how usage was calculated ended up counting tool output tokens, which caused quotas to drain way faster than expected. This wasn’t an intended change.\n\nThe team is rolling that back and reviewing refunds for anyone affected, and I’ll post again once that’s live. Thanks everyone for calling this out.\n\nZokor November 1, 2025, 8:27am 34\n\nKeep us posted, i just woke up and can’t work anymore due to a small prompt in the Pro subscription\n\njamesh November 1, 2025, 12:11pm 35\n\nStill waiting for OpenAI to fix the quota issues because I’m still stuck with a drained weekly quota. I think they just messed up and are claiming it’s a bug to be honest – no smoke tests were done to ensure there wasn’t a severe token bug, do they have a QA that even ran tests? It seems something this critical would have been easy to find.\n\nThey probably were testing the waters with this new token based system. To go from using unlimited from release, to gimped in one day, they didn’t think anyone would notice?\n\nBeen using TRAE for 48 hours and it’s been a great alternative.\n\ngeorgezip November 1, 2025, 3:27pm 36\n\nI haven’t had any quota restored yet, but token usage is reasonable now for me (Pro plan currently). I haven’t been able to use anywhere near the 5 hour quota so far.\n\nDebugN0mad November 1, 2025, 10:38pm 37\n\nKeep us posted with the updates.\n\ngeorgezip November 2, 2025, 2:18am 38\n\nMy weekly quota has been restored! Thanks OpenAI Support for making it right.\n\nMax_Zhadobin November 2, 2025, 3:35am 39\n\nSubject: Hit 5-hour limit in just 2 hours on Pro — and already at 35% of weekly cap\n\nHi team,\n\nI use Codex Web. After usage limits were introduced, I upgraded to Pro.\nToday, after about 2 hours of work, I suddenly hit the 5-hour limit and I’m already at 35% of the weekly limit.\n\nWhat’s confusing is that I’ve reduced my workload to stay within limits:\n\n  * I stopped running 4 parallel jobs; now I keep things mostly single-threaded.\n\n  * Overall task volume is roughly half of what it used to be.\n\nThis feels unfair, especially because Codex doesn’t produce perfect code and I often have to iterate and rerun tasks to fix issues — which naturally increases usage even for the same feature.\n\nCould you please clarify:\n\n  1. How Codex Web usage is measured/charged (per request, tokens, wall-clock time, retries, background work)?\n\n  2. Whether there’s a bug or recent change in accounting for Pro users.\n\n  3. If there’s a way to raise limits or get more transparent real-time usage breakdowns so we can plan work responsibly.\n\nThanks!\n\njayden_mitchell November 2, 2025, 4:38am 40\n\nCan you guys do something about this limit, it’s so annoying everything weas working nicely but on October 30th 2025 the limits got like so strict even on a paid pro account, i asked the chatgpt codex to do a few tasks and i was at 99% usage limit at the time and the tasks was barely a few hundred lines worth and then i went to go ask a follow up and evidently it says “Usage limit reached” and I came from a plus subscription because I thought this was an issue with plus only and upgrading did not solve it the usage limits are still as strict as ever, now I regret wasting $220 down the drain for this.\n\nCodex Credits Dissappearing\n\ngeorgezip November 2, 2025, 5:17am 41\n\nQuota calculation tweaks could still be in progress. Last night, I was only able to use less than 10-20% (IIRC) of 5-hour quota. Today, I was able to exhaust it.\n\nFor example:\n\nStarted with: 12% remaining of 5-hour quota; 74% weekly quota.\nRefactored a 4,379 line Python script.\nTook 46 minutes\nEnded with: 1% of 5-hour quota; 70% of weekly quota.\n\ngeorgezip November 2, 2025, 5:23am 42\n\n5-hour quota supposed to reset at 1:14 AM and it’s 1:27AM with no reset yet. Maybe some daylight savings time glitch?\n\n[Edit] it reset the second time 1:14am came around.\n\nR_R010 November 2, 2025, 7:05am 43\n\nThis happened again can we expect it to be reset again? It was working normally for last day and now it’s happening again. A few prompts and your through your daily limit.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nNews — Google DeepMind (https://deepmind.google/blog-categories/technical-blogs)\nciteturn1927search3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 7 months ago; ### Veo 3.1 Ingredients to Video: More consistency, creativity and control ... December 2025 Science ... November 2025 Research ... November 2025 Research\n\nLearn more\n\nEvals Publications Responsibility\n\n## Unlocking a new era of discovery with AI\n\nExplore science\n\nLife sciences\n\nAlphaFold Predict protein structures with high accuracy AlphaGenome Decode genetics to pinpoint diseases AlphaMissense Fin